cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the specific component and its original authors. This entry identifies
  the QuAntu collection; the report and Qiskit workshop have separate credits.
title: "QuAntü — Neutral-atom-based quantum computing in Chile (ATE250066)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "QuAntü Research Group"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ariel-Norambuena/QuAntu"
abstract: >-
  Research and educational collection of the ANID Thematic Research Ring project
  Neutral-atom-based quantum computing in Chile (ATE250066), organized into
  Algorithms, Experimental, and Theory groups. Includes rubidium D2 absorption spectroscopy,
  open quantum systems, magneto-optical trapping, and quantum computing.
  Historical numerical results and pending scientific validation are documented.
keywords:
  - rubidium
  - spectroscopy
  - open quantum systems
  - neutral atoms
  - quantum education
